Reading: the data PMP with the #78 two-word rule (8-byte accesses decided on both words, pmp_check_par) costs
~0.7 ns on the pmpaddr -> pmp_allow_data -> trap -> CSR-CE path, which moves from +1.517 to +0.803 ns and is
now the worst family after SHA-512, but nothing fails. The walker and fetch PMP checks stay above +2.6 ns.
The vstart EX hold (fd22878: reductions/vcpop/vfirst/vmsbf/viota/vcompress illegal when vstart != 0) adds no
failing or near-critical path: from vstart_q +2.376 ns, EX hold to IF/ID/ID/EX enables +3.668 ns.
If a later change eats the 0.8 ns, the first candidate is the data PMP -> trap -> CSR-CE fan-out.

